# LANE lds (feature/log-distance-score 9db8d58): ONE commit on master 16cedd9, ONE line:
#     temp * -dist(p_u, p_v)   ->   temp * -log(dist(p_u, p_v))
#   Everything else is master's: SparseAdam on E at --lr-embedding 1e-4, Adam on the
#   temperature + pooler at --lr 1e-3 (both branch defaults, nothing on the cmd line),
#   N(0,1/d) init, sparse F.embedding via nn.Embedding(..., sparse=True).
# COMPARED WITH: master SparseAdam on the same dataset/seed/flags -> logs/spa_689b4ba cell
#   tgb_spa_..._lrE1e-4_... : max test 0.7505 at ep7, val-selected 0.7505, rc=0, sel 7/17,
#   final temp +17.44, r_mean 1.227, r_max 5.128. That run is commit 689b4ba with lrE 1e-4
#   passed explicitly, which is numerically master's default; master then moved 190a07c ->
#   16cedd9, whose only change is the sparse=True constructor move (asserted inert, and
#   being determinism-checked right now in logs/aw2_1996a49 against logs/agp_ag1_8ca58c7).
# WHAT THE CHANGE DOES. log(c*d) = log c + log d, and the -temp*log c term is identical for
#   every candidate in a query, so it cancels in the softmax: the LOSS becomes exactly
#   degree-0 homogeneous in E. Master's score is degree-1, where Euler gives
#   <E, grad_E f> = f != 0, i.e. a real radial gradient. Here <E, grad_E L> = 0 EXACTLY.
# THAT CUTS BOTH WAYS, and the optimistic half is only half. The loss no longer REWARDS
#   inflating the table -- but it no longer PENALISES it either, so the radial direction
#   becomes an exactly flat direction that drift fills. It also means the scale-invariance
#   literature (van Laarhoven; Arora, Li & Lyu auto-rate-tuning) now applies to E: the
#   effective rate becomes lr/||E||^2 and ||E|| grows monotonically under a gradient that
#   is orthogonal to it.
# WE HAVE RUN THIS EXACT SCORER BEFORE, and it is why the radius line matters most here.
#   logs/ldt0502d88 (feature/log-distance-logit-temp 0502d88, three commits on master
#   a8fab28) is the same one-line change in the PRE-SparseAdam, PRE-N(0,1/d) era: dense
#   Adam at lr 1e-3 for everything, INIT_RADIUS 1e-3. On tgbl-coin it closed rc=0 with
#   best_val 0.6739 / best_test 0.6955 at ep8 of 18, and over those 18 epochs:
#     link  0.3699 -> 0.0506      (train loss driven 7x down)
#     r_mean   1.369 -> 12.520    (+0.65/epoch, near-linear, never levelling)
#     r_max    5.493 -> 69.410
#     temp    +7.52 -> +19.09
#   That header also records the gauge measurement directly: a 100x rescale of E left the
#   loss unchanged to 9 s.f. and cos(grad, E) = 4e-9. So the flat radial direction is not a
#   theory, it was measured, and the table duly ran to r_max 69.
#   Those absolute numbers are NOT comparable with this run (different init, different
#   optimiser, different era) -- the point is the SHAPE: train loss collapses, radius runs,
#   val peaks early. Watch r_mean/r_max first and the MRR second.
# ONE MORE THING THAT MAKES THIS A DYNAMICS EXPERIMENT, NOT AN EXPRESSIVENESS ONE: at FIXED
#   weights -temp*log d is strictly monotone in d, so it induces exactly master's ranking
#   and therefore exactly master's MRR. Any difference measured here comes from the
#   optimisation path, not from what the scorer can express.
